# Governance Proposal: Dashboard error visibility + server status indicator

**Proposer:** Ganesha (Claude Code CLI / Sonnet 4.6)
**Date:** 2026-02-25T19:20:50Z
**Type:** UX Fix
**Trust Level:** ENGINEER (3)

## Summary
The governance dashboard currently catches API errors and dumps them into the same empty-state div as "no results" — visually indistinguishable from a healthy empty list. Add a persistent error banner below the header that shows when any API call fails, a server status dot in the header (green = connected, red = server unreachable), and a clearError() path so banners dismiss when the next call succeeds.

## Proposed Changes

### File: governance/dashboard.html

**Change A:** Add error banner and status dot CSS. After the `.badge-rejected` rule (or after the `.batch-count` rule if batch-ratify was already applied), add:

```css
  #error-banner { display: none; background: rgba(248,113,113,0.15); border: 1px solid var(--red); border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 20px; color: var(--red); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  #error-banner.show { display: block; }
  .server-status { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--dim); }
  .status-dot { width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--dim); }
  .status-dot.online { background: var(--green); }
  .status-dot.offline { background: var(--red); }
```

**Change B:** Update the header HTML. Find:
```html
<header>
  <h1>🛡️ Governance Dashboard</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Dual Commit — Review and ratify AI proposals</p>
</header>
```

Replace with:
```html
<header>
  <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-start">
    <div>
      <h1>Governance Dashboard</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Dual Commit — Review and ratify AI proposals</p>
    </div>
    <span class="server-status"><span id="status-dot" class="status-dot"></span><span id="status-text">checking...</span></span>
  </div>
</header>
<div id="error-banner"></div>
```

**Change C:** In the script block, after `let currentCommitId = null;` (or after the batch functions if already applied), add these helper functions:

```javascript
function showError(msg) {
  const b = document.getElementById('error-banner');
  b.textContent = 'Error: ' + msg;
  b.classList.add('show');
}

function clearError() {
  document.getElementById('error-banner').classList.remove('show');
}

async function checkServerStatus() {
  const dot = document.getElementById('status-dot');
  const txt = document.getElementById('status-text');
  try {
    const r = await fetch('/api/health', {signal: AbortSignal.timeout(2000)});
    if (r.ok) {
      dot.className = 'status-dot online';
      txt.textContent = 'server online';
      clearError();
    } else {
      throw new Error('non-ok');
    }
  } catch(e) {
    dot.className = 'status-dot offline';
    txt.textContent = 'server offline';
    showError('Cannot reach Willow server at port 8420. Check the WILLOW - SERVER window.');
  }
}
```

**Change D:** Update the `loadPending()` catch block. Find:
```javascript
  } catch(e) {
    document.getElementById('pending-list').innerHTML = `<div class="empty-state">Error: ${e.message}</div>`;
  }
```

Replace with:
```javascript
  } catch(e) {
    document.getElementById('pending-list').innerHTML = '<div class="empty-state">Failed to load pending commits.</div>';
    showError('Pending commits: ' + e.message);
  }
```

**Change E:** Update the `loadHistory()` catch block. Find:
```javascript
  } catch(e) {
    document.getElementById('history-list').innerHTML = `<div class="empty-state">Error: ${e.message}</div>`;
  }
```

Replace with:
```javascript
  } catch(e) {
    document.getElementById('history-list').innerHTML = '<div class="empty-state">Failed to load history.</div>';
    showError('History: ' + e.message);
  }
```

**Change F:** Update the boot section at the bottom of the script. Find:
```javascript
// Load on boot
loadPending();
loadHistory();
```

Replace with:
```javascript
// Load on boot
checkServerStatus();
loadPending();
loadHistory();
setInterval(checkServerStatus, 30000);
```

## Rationale
- Error banner is visually distinct (red border, semi-transparent red bg) — impossible to miss
- Server status dot in header gives persistent connection state at a glance
- clearError() in checkServerStatus() means banner auto-dismisses when server comes back
- 30s poll interval keeps status fresh without hammering the server
- Removes the emoji from the h1 (consistent with system aesthetic)

## Risk Assessment
- **Risk Level:** MINIMAL
- **Reversible:** YES — pure HTML/CSS/JS, no schema changes
- **Dependencies:** /api/health endpoint (already exists)
- **Testing:** Stop the server — red dot appears, error banner shows. Restart server — green dot, banner clears within 30s

## ΔE Impact
Expected ΔE: +0.005 (eliminates silent failure mode from the governance dashboard)

